WEBVTT

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:41.200
Dragoon!

00:01:45.260 --> 00:01:50.380
Kane's digital Sacred Beast evolved to
the point of consuming the entire tower.

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:53.770
Takao and the rest of
us were in bad shape.

00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:58.580
Let's do this, Seiryu!

00:01:58.580 --> 00:02:02.400
Dragoon and Seiryu
saved the day for us.

00:02:07.830 --> 00:02:10.920
Go, Dragoon!

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:16.990
By fighting as one,
Takao and Seiryu

00:02:16.990 --> 00:02:22.600
finally defeated Kane, the digital Sacred Beast,
and the rest of Gideon's group!

00:02:32.710 --> 00:02:36.390
It's been a little bit since then.

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:42.900
We left Japan for the time being and
are heading to New York, USA!

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:47.320
Would you like something to drink?

00:02:50.090 --> 00:02:52.630
One milk, please.

00:02:52.630 --> 00:02:54.970
Sure. Here you are.

00:02:54.970 --> 00:02:56.320
Thank you.

00:02:57.630 --> 00:03:03.700
Max's mom, Judy,
invited us to America.

00:03:04.830 --> 00:03:12.250
Our Beyblades were damaged in the Battle Tower, so we're getting maintenance done at Judy's facilities.

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:17.710
But this vacation is the
best present of all.

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:30.670
For crying out loud!

00:03:30.670 --> 00:03:32.990
You're really hanging in there.

00:03:35.010 --> 00:03:40.820
I figured you'd usually have
forced him awake by now.

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:43.090
I really want to.

00:03:43.460 --> 00:03:49.760
But Takao can finally take a breather
now that our battle with Psykick is done.

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:54.480
I figured I'd at least let
him relax on this vacation.

00:03:55.130 --> 00:04:00.130
How nice! I didn't think
you had it in you, Hiromi!

00:04:00.130 --> 00:04:01.440
Aww, jeez...

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:04.070
What's that supposed to mean?!

00:04:05.370 --> 00:04:08.960
Shut up! Can't a guy get a
little sleep around here?!

00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:14.790
You've been sound asleep
since we left Japan!

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:17.720
Oh, I have? Oh well!

00:04:17.720 --> 00:04:21.040
I'm gonna have a blast once we land!

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:23.700
Someone sure is happy...

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:26.780
I'm sure Kai came along to
enjoy a vacation too, right?

00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:31.420
Or not, I guess.

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:35.670
Kai's just here to get
maintenance on Dranzer.

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:37.840
He's not interested
in anything else.

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:42.300
Or so he says! I bet he brought
along his swim trunks, too.

00:04:43.150 --> 00:04:44.740
Well, Kai?

00:04:44.740 --> 00:04:46.690
Oh, stop! He's asleep!

00:04:46.690 --> 00:04:47.460
It's fine!

00:04:48.460 --> 00:04:50.240
I haven't been to America in six months...

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:52.780
I'll be able to see mom soon!

00:05:04.980 --> 00:05:06.050
Max!

00:05:07.890 --> 00:05:09.220
Mom!

00:05:10.270 --> 00:05:11.960
Welcome home, Max!

00:05:11.960 --> 00:05:13.800
I missed you, mom!

00:05:13.800 --> 00:05:19.410
Genbu got taken by some bad
guys back in Japan! It was horrible!

00:05:19.410 --> 00:05:23.480
I heard all about Psykick
in Kyoujyu's e-mail.

00:05:23.480 --> 00:05:25.580
I was so worried!

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:29.260
Thank you for bringing us over, Judy!

00:05:29.260 --> 00:05:31.060
Looking forward to it!

00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:34.250
Um, nice to meet you!
I'm Hiromi Tachibana!

00:05:34.250 --> 00:05:38.550
My, what a cute little lady!
Welcome to New York!

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:56.340
New York sure brings back memories!

00:05:56.340 --> 00:05:58.870
We haven't been back since
the American tournament!

00:05:58.870 --> 00:06:02.900
This city has been reborn after
going through some tough ordeals.

00:06:02.900 --> 00:06:08.300
No matter how hard we get beat down we get
right up. That resilient energy is our pride.

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:13.410
Hey, mom, you said there was something you
wanted to show us in your lab, right?

00:06:13.410 --> 00:06:16.010
Yes, something very rare.

00:06:16.010 --> 00:06:18.200
What is it?

00:06:18.460 --> 00:06:25.090
It's something I'm sure will gain attention
all across America, no, the world.

00:06:25.090 --> 00:06:27.570
Something with a mysterious power within it.

00:06:27.870 --> 00:06:31.370
It's actually related to all of you.

00:06:31.370 --> 00:06:32.960
To us?

00:06:32.960 --> 00:06:34.080
Yes.

00:06:48.070 --> 00:06:51.340
Here we not only do
developmental research,

00:06:51.340 --> 00:06:54.820
but we also research the
energy emitted from Beyblades.

00:06:58.630 --> 00:07:01.300
The facilities are as
amazing as I remember.

00:07:01.300 --> 00:07:05.620
I really want to see this
mysterious power thingy!

00:07:05.620 --> 00:07:07.520
It sounds so interesting, right?

00:07:07.520 --> 00:07:08.930
It's just ahead.

00:07:19.990 --> 00:07:23.330
This is off limits to
everyone except researchers.

00:07:23.330 --> 00:07:25.010
You kids are special.

00:07:25.010 --> 00:07:27.720
I'm getting kinda excited!

00:07:31.950 --> 00:07:34.060
I can't see anything.

00:07:34.460 --> 00:07:35.820
Lights, please.

00:07:42.080 --> 00:07:43.380
It's a stone tablet.

00:07:43.380 --> 00:07:45.080
It looks rather ancient.

00:07:45.080 --> 00:07:50.640
This is a stone tablet that was discovered
in the Mexican deserts 20 years ago.

00:07:50.640 --> 00:07:54.380
Until recently, it was under military supervision.

00:07:55.360 --> 00:07:58.250
It just looks like any old rock to me.

00:07:58.250 --> 00:08:00.730
How about this, then?

00:08:05.530 --> 00:08:07.280
Look at this, please.

00:08:10.610 --> 00:08:11.900
What's this?

00:08:11.900 --> 00:08:13.240
Those are characters!

00:08:13.240 --> 00:08:18.880
We believe it's an ancient language that
goes further back than the Incan Empire.

00:08:18.880 --> 00:08:21.330
We're in the middle of deciphering it.

00:08:21.330 --> 00:08:25.030
But what does this
have to do with us?

00:08:29.200 --> 00:08:30.960
Begin the experiment.

00:08:43.920 --> 00:08:45.540
They're going to battle?

00:08:45.780 --> 00:08:46.970
Three.

00:08:46.970 --> 00:08:48.050
Two.

00:08:48.050 --> 00:08:49.040
One.

00:08:49.040 --> 00:08:50.800
Go Shoot!

00:08:53.040 --> 00:08:59.810
The Bey that the robot launched has a
piece of the stone tablet equipped in it.

00:09:00.390 --> 00:09:02.720
It has part of the stone in the Bit?

00:09:02.720 --> 00:09:03.980
Just watch.

00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:15.620
Is this a...

00:09:16.020 --> 00:09:17.520
Sacred Beast?!

00:09:26.490 --> 00:09:28.380
Hey, you okay?

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:30.090
Are you hurt?

00:09:36.210 --> 00:09:40.270
That light... It definitely
looked like a Sacred Beast.

00:09:40.270 --> 00:09:41.300
It was.

00:09:41.840 --> 00:09:44.700
More accurately, it's an
incomplete Sacred Beast.

00:09:44.700 --> 00:09:47.400
Incomplete? How?

00:09:47.400 --> 00:09:49.510
The secret is in this stone tablet.

00:09:49.510 --> 00:09:56.210
Under the right conditions, it can bring
something akin to a Sacred Beast to life.

00:09:56.210 --> 00:10:04.580
What?! Does this mean that you could make Beyblades with Sacred Beasts in them just like that?

00:10:04.580 --> 00:10:05.730
What?!

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:08.970
It's hard to say.

00:10:09.250 --> 00:10:15.900
Even now, a Beyblade exploded with
just a piece of the stone inside of it.

00:10:19.420 --> 00:10:22.420
But theoretically, it is possible.

00:10:22.610 --> 00:10:25.780
Is that where all Sacred
Beasts come from, mom?

00:10:25.780 --> 00:10:29.680
That's what we want to know,
so we're continuing our research.

00:10:29.680 --> 00:10:34.570
What is a Sacred Beast?
Where does their energy come from?

00:10:34.570 --> 00:10:39.070
It's surely connected to the Sacred
Beasts in your Beyblades.

00:10:39.070 --> 00:10:45.540
What wonderful research! Please
allow me to help in any way I can!

00:10:45.540 --> 00:10:49.810
Thank you. But to be honest,
there's one aspect I am worried about.

00:10:49.810 --> 00:10:51.860
Something you're worried about?

00:10:52.290 --> 00:10:54.820
According to FBI intelligence,

00:10:54.820 --> 00:11:00.110
there's an international crime group with
their sights set on this stone tablet.

00:11:00.110 --> 00:11:01.180
What?!

00:11:01.180 --> 00:11:04.210
For obvious reasons, I imagine.

00:11:04.640 --> 00:11:08.050
We have to rely on the
highest level of security.

00:11:08.640 --> 00:11:11.750
So that's how important this is.

00:11:12.050 --> 00:11:15.770
Whoa! Do I know you?

00:11:16.640 --> 00:11:18.360
Hey, Max!

00:11:18.360 --> 00:11:19.930
Allen!

00:11:19.930 --> 00:11:22.290
It's been ages!

00:11:22.750 --> 00:11:23.910
How've you been?

00:11:23.910 --> 00:11:25.230
It's good to see you!

00:12:00.720 --> 00:12:03.040
Oh, darn!
How irritating!

00:12:13.170 --> 00:12:15.010
Kyoujyu, what are you doing?!

00:12:15.330 --> 00:12:17.490
I wanted to try it,
at least just once.

00:12:17.490 --> 00:12:20.560
The police are gonna bust you...

00:12:20.560 --> 00:12:21.980
Really?

00:12:25.080 --> 00:12:26.960
I'm so sorry!

00:12:34.120 --> 00:12:39.700
That's tasty! But to think you'd
become a researcher at my mom's lab!

00:12:39.700 --> 00:12:41.190
It's a total surprise!

00:12:41.190 --> 00:12:43.340
I just had interest in Beyblades.

00:12:43.340 --> 00:12:46.870
You were always better
than me at school stuff.

00:12:46.870 --> 00:12:52.890
I tried to catch up, but when it came to
school and sports, I was no match for you.

00:12:52.890 --> 00:12:56.310
We competed over the
dumbest stuff, though.

00:12:56.310 --> 00:12:57.490
Yeah!

00:12:57.910 --> 00:13:00.480
We went at it,
no matter what it was!

00:13:00.480 --> 00:13:02.980
Rivals in everything!

00:13:02.980 --> 00:13:05.200
That sure takes me back.

00:13:05.410 --> 00:13:09.100
But you were the better Beyblader.

00:13:12.660 --> 00:13:15.950
I didn't have anything
else going for me!

00:13:15.950 --> 00:13:20.130
You see, there's a Beyblade
tournament around here tomorrow.

00:13:20.130 --> 00:13:21.750
I'm entered in.

00:13:21.750 --> 00:13:23.580
You are? Wow!

00:13:23.580 --> 00:13:26.280
Would you like to enter, too?

00:13:26.610 --> 00:13:27.490
Can I?

00:13:27.490 --> 00:13:31.960
Of course! It'll be a special
entry from the BBA team!

00:13:31.960 --> 00:13:34.550
Okay, okay! How exciting!

00:13:34.550 --> 00:13:38.120
We might even get
to battle each other!

00:13:39.250 --> 00:13:41.010
I can't wait!

00:14:24.540 --> 00:14:34.490
"Bakuten Shoot Beyblade 2002"

00:14:48.720 --> 00:14:52.920
Here's Driger and Dranzer.
Maintenance complete.

00:14:56.760 --> 00:14:58.110
Where's Dragoon?

00:14:58.250 --> 00:15:03.050
There's more damage on Dragoon
and Draciel than we expected, so...

00:15:03.050 --> 00:15:06.900
What?! I'm not gonna make it
to tomorrow's match, then!

00:15:07.310 --> 00:15:09.580
I knew you'd say that.

00:15:11.590 --> 00:15:13.020
Dad!

00:15:14.060 --> 00:15:17.370
Someone sure is excited to see me!

00:15:17.370 --> 00:15:19.760
It's been so long since I've seen you!

00:15:19.760 --> 00:15:21.640
I'm even a little taller, Dad!

00:15:21.640 --> 00:15:22.880
I see!

00:15:22.880 --> 00:15:26.600
I asked him to lend a hand
with Dragoon's repairs.

00:15:26.600 --> 00:15:27.360
What?

00:15:27.880 --> 00:15:32.430
Unfortunately, it's not just the
Attack Ring and Weight Disk.

00:15:32.430 --> 00:15:35.020
The core parts are
damaged as well.

00:15:35.020 --> 00:15:36.330
What does that mean?

00:15:36.330 --> 00:15:38.010
Don't worry.

00:15:38.010 --> 00:15:42.450
With my skills,
I'll have it good as new in no time!

00:15:42.450 --> 00:15:43.990
Yes!

00:15:45.020 --> 00:15:48.010
Here. You can use this Bey for practice.

00:15:48.010 --> 00:15:49.290
Thank you!

00:15:49.290 --> 00:15:52.710
Time to take Driger
out for a test spin.

00:15:53.230 --> 00:15:55.480
Kai. Let's battle.

00:15:55.950 --> 00:15:59.930
Are you sure? Don't blame me if
you end up needing more repairs.

00:15:59.930 --> 00:16:01.870
Let's cut the trash talk
and get on with it!

00:16:01.870 --> 00:16:03.740
This'll be good!

00:16:05.120 --> 00:16:07.920
Are you two ready?
Here we go!

00:16:07.920 --> 00:16:09.090
Three!

00:16:09.250 --> 00:16:10.460
Two!

00:16:10.590 --> 00:16:11.600
One!

00:16:11.600 --> 00:16:14.020
Go Shoot!

00:16:19.390 --> 00:16:21.740
Their movements are so neat! Their speed!

00:16:22.530 --> 00:16:26.180
Both of them have
improved quite a bit!

00:16:26.180 --> 00:16:28.740
Darn it!
Let me in on this, too!

00:16:28.740 --> 00:16:30.640
Director! It's an emergency!

00:16:30.910 --> 00:16:31.920
What's the matter?

00:16:31.920 --> 00:16:34.620
The stone tablet!
It's been stolen!

00:16:50.700 --> 00:16:52.670
They don't know when to quit.

00:17:24.700 --> 00:17:27.880
I'm Scott from the NYPD.
You're Judy, yes?

00:17:27.880 --> 00:17:28.960
Yes.

00:17:28.960 --> 00:17:32.890
Our surveillance systems have
been hacked from the inside.

00:17:33.150 --> 00:17:34.870
But how...?

00:17:34.870 --> 00:17:36.260
Hey! Old dude!

00:17:36.260 --> 00:17:38.730
Where'd the guys who
stole the tablet go?

00:17:38.730 --> 00:17:41.740
"Old dude"?! Who do you
think you're talking to?

00:17:44.120 --> 00:17:47.440
Ignore him, he's just a tourist!

00:17:47.440 --> 00:17:49.710
Lemme go!

00:17:50.270 --> 00:17:53.420
The suspect's car is
heading down 42nd.

00:17:53.420 --> 00:17:56.330
We've ordered our patrol
to stay in pursuit.

00:17:58.670 --> 00:18:00.270
Max! Hop in!

00:18:00.270 --> 00:18:01.270
Dad!

00:18:01.270 --> 00:18:03.640
We're getting back
your mom's tablet!

00:18:03.640 --> 00:18:04.660
Dad!

00:18:06.560 --> 00:18:07.560
Max!

00:18:07.560 --> 00:18:09.400
Wait! I'm coming too!

00:18:12.670 --> 00:18:15.390
Crap! In that case...

00:18:18.110 --> 00:18:19.600
Hey, you!

00:18:19.600 --> 00:18:21.310
I'm borrowing this!

00:18:28.290 --> 00:18:30.380
There's no end to 'em.

00:18:30.890 --> 00:18:32.480
Suck on this!

00:18:46.020 --> 00:18:46.970
Dad...

00:18:46.970 --> 00:18:48.760
We're blocked.

00:18:49.350 --> 00:18:52.450
Wait up, you jerks!

00:18:56.920 --> 00:18:58.630
Wait up!!

00:19:03.330 --> 00:19:04.670
Takao!

00:19:05.660 --> 00:19:11.590
Hang on, Max! I'm gonna catch these
thieves for you and your mom!

00:19:15.210 --> 00:19:18.760
Are you saying that one of our
own led the perpetrator in?

00:19:18.760 --> 00:19:20.940
I simply cannot believe that!

00:19:20.940 --> 00:19:24.570
After our investigation,
the details should come to light.

00:19:24.570 --> 00:19:29.020
And, well, this is still
unconfirmed, but...

00:19:29.370 --> 00:19:33.480
Japan seems to be the home base of
this international criminal organization...

00:19:33.700 --> 00:19:34.880
--What?!

00:19:35.240 --> 00:19:36.860
Is that true?

00:19:36.860 --> 00:19:39.020
Stay out of this, you kids!

00:19:39.510 --> 00:19:43.350
Inspector, according to one of
our patrol cars on the scene,

00:19:43.350 --> 00:19:45.610
We've got someone on
the chase of the suspects.

00:19:46.510 --> 00:19:48.650
Send the entire city's
patrol cars their way.

00:19:48.650 --> 00:19:52.760
According to eyewitnesses,
it's just one boy on a bicycle.

00:19:52.760 --> 00:19:54.510
W-what?!

00:19:54.510 --> 00:19:55.910
--Takao!

00:20:03.100 --> 00:20:05.100
Now no one'll be able to...

00:20:05.860 --> 00:20:08.320
Stop, dammit!

00:20:12.270 --> 00:20:14.130
Takao Kinomiya...

00:20:18.550 --> 00:20:20.440
Go!

00:20:34.260 --> 00:20:35.600
Book it!

00:20:37.950 --> 00:20:40.410
Stop, darn you!

00:20:49.890 --> 00:20:51.050
Max!

00:20:51.670 --> 00:20:52.600
What...?

00:20:53.310 --> 00:20:54.870
Allen?

00:20:54.870 --> 00:20:56.370
Is that you, Allen?

00:20:58.560 --> 00:20:59.560
Max...

00:20:59.560 --> 00:21:01.820
Allen? What are you doing?

00:21:01.820 --> 00:21:05.440
Max! He's one of the
guys who stole the tablet!

00:21:05.440 --> 00:21:07.230
Stop him!

00:21:14.040 --> 00:21:16.970
Max! Why didn't you stop him?

00:21:16.970 --> 00:21:19.820
I said he was one of the thieves!

00:21:24.230 --> 00:21:25.950
Max, what's wrong?

00:21:27.640 --> 00:21:29.000
Allen...

00:22:59.460 --> 00:23:04.310
Max catches his friend Allen at the scene with the group who stole the stone tablet.

00:23:04.310 --> 00:23:09.060
Max takes on Allen to find out what happened.

00:23:09.060 --> 00:23:12.410
Yes! It's going to be an All-en out battle!

00:23:12.410 --> 00:23:17.580
Chairman! You can't just make bad jokes all the way from Japan!

00:23:17.580 --> 00:23:21.120
Pay Max-imum attention to the next episode, too!
